    "title": "Is Brock Lesnar retiring? WWE stars hints end at WrestleMania 42",
    "text": "April 19, 2026Updated April 22, 2026, 12:53 p.m. ETLAS VEGAS — Is Brock Lesnar done?\"The Beast Incarnate\" took on Oba Femi at night two of WrestleMania 42 on Sunday, April 19, pitting a battle of heavyweights in the longtime star vs. the future of the business.It was a sight Lesnar hadn't seen much. After hitting him with his signature F5, Femi got right up and surprised him with a slam. He then delivered a powerbomb to slam Lesnar into the ring. He gets the pin and slays the \"Beast Incarnate.\"It was a win that showed how dominant Femi is, showing how easy he could take down even one of the biggest stars in the business. But that wasn't all.After losing, Lesnar took off his gloves and began to cry. The crowd realized what was happening, almost in shock, as Lesnar took off his boots, unable to hide the tears.Typically, that signals a wrestler is calling it a career. Longtime manager Paul Heyman entered the ring and the two shared an embrace, with Heyman holding his arm in the air as the crowd gives him an ovation. Lesnar then salutes the crowd and actually gives thanks to some of the fans ringside, seemingly waving goodbye.It's not officially been said, but it appears Lesnar is retiring from WWE, something that was expected to happen in the near future, but not at WrestleMania.",
